// EXPECT: FAIL
// ERROR_CONTAINS: ANUBIS_ASSERTION_DISPROVED
// Mixed-theory assert decomposition: a conjunction `A && B` whose conjuncts live in DIFFERENT solver
// lanes (a string equality `s == "a"` and an integer equality `1 == 2`) used to match no single lane
// and pass vacuously (deferred wholesale to the runtime) — a fail-open where even a modelable-FALSE
// conjunct slipped past `check`. The assert is now DECOMPOSED and each conjunct discharged in its own
// lane (`assert(A && B)` iff `assert(A)` ∧ `assert(B)`), so the provably-false `1 == 2` conjunct is
// disproved at compile time and the check rejects. Splitting only adds obligations, so it can never
// introduce a false accept.
fn f(s: string) requires(s == "a") {
    assert(s == "a" && 1 == 2);
}
fn main() { f("a"); }
